      "questions": [
        {
          "id": 2001,
          "order": 1,
          "question_type": "READING",
          "is_math_input": false,
          "question_text": "<p>Marine biologist Ayesha Rahman spent three seasons recording the clicks of sperm whales off the coast of Dominica. She noticed that whales in the same family group repeated a short pattern of clicks, called a <em>coda</em>, far more often than whales from other groups did. Rahman argues that these shared codas work much like a family name: they let a whale signal which group it belongs to.</p>",
          "question_prompt": "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?",
          "question_image_key": null,
          "options": {
            "A": {
              "text": "Rahman found that sperm whales can only communicate with members of their own family group.",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "B": {
              "text": "Rahman's recordings suggest that sperm whales use shared click patterns to identify their group.",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "C": {
              "text": "Rahman discovered that codas are learned from whales in other family groups.",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "D": {
              "text": "Rahman concluded that sperm whales stop producing codas once they leave the coast of Dominica.",
              "image_key": null
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 2002,
          "order": 2,
          "question_type": "WRITING",
          "is_math_input": false,
          "question_text": "<p>In 1921 the chemist Alice Ball developed a way to make chaulmoogra oil dissolve in water, producing the first injectable treatment for leprosy that the body could absorb. Her method ______ for more than two decades, until antibiotics replaced it in the 1940s.</p>",
          "question_prompt": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
          "question_image_key": null,
          "options": {
            "A": {
              "text": "was used",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "B": {
              "text": "were used",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "C": {
              "text": "have been used",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "D": {
              "text": "being used",
              "image_key": null
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 2003,
          "order": 3,
          "question_type": "READING",
          "is_math_input": false,
          "question_text": "<p>Many cities plant trees along streets to cool neighborhoods in summer. <u>A 2024 survey of twelve cities, however, found that newly planted trees lowered street temperatures only after their canopies had grown for at least eight years.</u> Planners who expect quick results may therefore be disappointed, even though the long-term benefits are well documented.</p>",
          "question_prompt": "Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?",
          "question_image_key": null,
          "options": {
            "A": {
              "text": "It introduces a finding that qualifies the expectation described in the first sentence.",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "B": {
              "text": "It provides an example of a city that stopped planting trees.",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "C": {
              "text": "It explains why the long-term benefits of trees are well documented.",
              "image_key": null
            },
            "D": {
              "text": "It describes a method planners use to choose which trees to plant.",
              "image_key": null
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 2004,
          "order": 4,
          "question_type": "READING",
          "is_math_input": false,
          "question_text": "<p>A beekeeping cooperative tracked how many of its monitored colonies were lost each winter.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Winter</th><th>Colonies monitored</th><th>Colonies lost (%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2021&ndash;22</td><td>420</td><td>31</td></tr><tr><td>2022&ndash;23</td><td>455</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><td>2023&ndash;24</td><td>470</td><td>18</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The cooperative attributes the change to a new practice of insulating hives each autumn, which it began in 2022.</p>",
